{"custom_id": "2c238df8ecf9f84fd17aec36a296f02ff6e511cc4f26d2db", "meta": {"loop": "topk4L01", "task": "generate_moderation_principle_1", "occurrence": 0, "attempt": 0, "prompt_sha256": "f14d72e21cb707b402b8799df0fc927dba713169dbf2ea35ad2a88a6ea8d4df7", "prompt_chars": 5528}, "batch_id": "msgbatch_01MQLvDoTh446B65fGF8QSTv", "saved_utc": "2026-10-22T09:54:34+00:00", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgH53AfbesNCYsZkMQCJb", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Privative Loss-of-Function Span Rule:** IF a noun phrase contains a privative state head (a deficiency, absence, lack, or deficient-activity nominal) whose argument is a molecular entity (gene, enzyme, protein, or protein component), AND the phrase names a patient-level disorder under an etiological, symptom, or patient-presence frame (e.g., \"caused by,\" \"characterized by,\" \"responsible for,\" \"presenting as,\" \"in a patient with\"), THEN label the complete span (head, complement, and any premodifying or parenthetical acronym that belongs to the same term) as SpecificDisease. Never label only the molecular argument, and never split the head from its complement.\n  - **Does NOT apply** when the privative word is an adjective describing a phenotype, carrier status, or genotype-level attribute (e.g., \"deficient phenotype\"); label that as Modifier.\n  - **Does NOT apply** when the phrase quantifies a degree, amount, or level of reduced activity or yield (numeric values, percentages, \"reduced yield,\" \"% of normal\"); keep these as O.\n  - **Does NOT apply** when the molecular term appears in a purely biochemical or mechanistic statement that names no condition and no affected patient; keep these as O.\n  - **Defer to CompositeMention conventions** when the privative phrase is one member of a coordinated list of conditions.\n  - **Generalization:** The rule depends on the structural relation between a privative head and a molecular argument, not on any particular noun, verb, or enzyme name, so it covers unseen enzymes, proteins, and phrasings.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2219, "output_tokens": 2782, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2252}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}